WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:05.150
- It is a welcome and a joy
to say hi to Julianne Moore.

00:00:05.419 --> 00:00:07.770
(audience clapping)

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:09.630
Hi, you are so beautiful.

00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:11.550
You look so good.

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:13.680
Congratulations on your show.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:14.740
I'm so happy for you.

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:15.573
- Thank you.

00:00:15.573 --> 00:00:20.573
Spoken by the woman who
literally is my beauty style,

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:23.330
hair, eyes, skin, nose, face,

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:26.059
and decorative icon, by the way.

00:00:26.059 --> 00:00:26.950
- Thank you.

00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:28.020
- We'll get into that.

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:31.470
But your family, like your love story

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:34.080
with your husband is
such relationship goals.

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:37.610
And I know you just posted
something about your anniversary.

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:41.640
And I remember years ago,
hearing you two got together,

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:44.540
you had made this film,
and you fell in love.

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:49.540
And I just, your love story
is such relationship goals.

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:51.050
- Well, I will tell you,

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:52.360
you know what's really funny about it?

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:55.080
Is that you say years
ago, it was 24 years ago.

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:56.540
That's what's shocking to us.

00:00:56.540 --> 00:00:58.660
We're like we met 24 years ago?

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:01.690
- Can I ask you a weird personal question?

00:01:01.690 --> 00:01:04.110
Like you and your husband are so amazing,

00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:05.670
Like, do you have any tips

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:10.400
for people on like an
awesome, like union marriage?

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:12.160
Like, do you have a secret?

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:13.830
Do you have something to turn to?

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:17.480
Like, I think a lot of us, you know,

00:01:17.480 --> 00:01:20.623
would love to know if you
have any tips or insights.

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:24.690
- I think, I mean, the
only thing that I can say,

00:01:24.690 --> 00:01:28.040
I think that you both have
to really want to be married.

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:31.260
I do, feel like I've seen situations

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:32.820
where things aren't
working out for people,

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:36.870
because one of the, one of the members

00:01:36.870 --> 00:01:39.630
of the couple doesn't want to be there.

00:01:39.630 --> 00:01:43.490
So, I think if you're both
invested in it working out,

00:01:43.490 --> 00:01:45.830
and that, and that's important,

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:47.740
and then you really have
to have a good time.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:49.180
My God you have to,

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:51.110
I think they really
have to make you laugh.

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:53.533
If they don't make you
laugh, it's just deadly.

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:56.050
And somebody asked me the other day

00:01:56.050 --> 00:01:57.530
if it felt like a long time.

00:01:57.530 --> 00:01:59.790
And I was like, oddly, no, it doesn't.

00:01:59.790 --> 00:02:02.070
I mean, I think that's
what's been nice about it.

00:02:02.070 --> 00:02:03.330
It doesn't feel like a long time.

00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:07.890
And, but now, I mean, our kids
are, our kids are 18 and 22.

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:09.600
How old are your kids now?

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:12.580
- They're six, Frankie's
six, she'll be seven,

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:15.949
and Olive turns eight,
like any second, so.

00:02:15.949 --> 00:02:16.840
- Oh my goodness.

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:17.673
- I know.

00:02:17.673 --> 00:02:19.718
- Are they in school virtually?

00:02:19.718 --> 00:02:20.551
They must be.

00:02:20.551 --> 00:02:22.540
- No, they went back.

00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:25.470
So, and I had such a struggle with it

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:27.610
because as a parent, I wasn't sure.

00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:29.370
And for the show's sake, I was worried

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:30.750
about what they were
going to bring back in.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:31.860
But then I thought, oh my God,

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:35.240
what a Hollywood stage
nightmare mother I would be,

00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:36.250
like, you can't go to school

00:02:36.250 --> 00:02:38.758
because mom can't get sick at her job.

00:02:38.758 --> 00:02:40.523
(Julianne laughing) So
I was like, guess what?

00:02:40.523 --> 00:02:41.780
We're just rolling the dice.

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:44.680
Because every time you try
to plan, it's so terrifying,

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:46.610
and everything keeps
having to pivot anyway.

00:02:46.610 --> 00:02:50.070
So I feel like it's almost
rude to wrestle anymore,

00:02:50.070 --> 00:02:50.903
and just succumb.

00:02:50.903 --> 00:02:53.810
Well, you know, my daughter
was a camp counselor

00:02:53.810 --> 00:02:56.060
at this little camp, you
know, that she went to

00:02:56.060 --> 00:02:57.790
when she was a kid, she was
always a camp counselor there,

00:02:57.790 --> 00:03:00.180
and she had three and four old girls,

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:02.310
and the counselors all wore masks,

00:03:02.310 --> 00:03:04.110
but the kids didn't cause
they were too little,

00:03:04.110 --> 00:03:05.370
and everybody was fine.

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:06.280
They were all okay.

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:08.610
And those little kids were
all over her, you know?

00:03:08.610 --> 00:03:11.650
So, I do think with testing
and everything like that,

00:03:11.650 --> 00:03:13.540
things can be done safely, but it's hard.

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:14.400
It's really hard.

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:17.250
- I know all of a sudden
the hug has so much

00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:19.700
more than just a hug.

00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:21.230
Like, will I get sick hugging you?

00:03:21.230 --> 00:03:22.350
Will I make you sick?

00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:24.610
This is a lot going into a quick hug.

00:03:24.610 --> 00:03:27.493
Oh wait, is your daughter on Tik Tok?

00:03:28.379 --> 00:03:29.633
- Yeah.

00:03:30.930 --> 00:03:33.200
- Have you joined her for some Tik Tok?

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:36.070
- There might've been a
couple, but you know, nothing.

00:03:36.070 --> 00:03:37.778
I don't, I'm, oh no.

00:03:37.778 --> 00:03:39.230
Yeah, there might've been something.

00:03:39.230 --> 00:03:42.370
I think there was one where
I was doing the dishes

00:03:42.370 --> 00:03:43.680
and she went, it was some Tik Tok

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:45.260
where you supposed to like do something

00:03:45.260 --> 00:03:46.460
with your mom or something.

00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:49.290
Anyway, I participated in
that without my knowledge.

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:54.290
- I'm excited that we both
have a love of design.

00:03:54.550 --> 00:03:56.370
- Yes, yes, absolutely.

00:03:56.370 --> 00:03:58.136
It's my hobby.

00:03:58.136 --> 00:03:59.620
It's my big hobby.

00:03:59.620 --> 00:04:01.720
- Where did it all start for you?

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:03.210
The love of design.

00:04:03.210 --> 00:04:05.050
- It was my mother, you know?

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:08.250
I mean, I don't think I realized
how much I was absorbing

00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:09.700
from her, but she was the kind of person

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:11.620
who really cared how things looked.

00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:14.330
And she, you know, my
parents were students

00:04:14.330 --> 00:04:16.250
for a really long time, so
they never had any money.

00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:19.050
So she would do things like
make her own slip covers,

00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:22.230
just always sewing things, and
refinish furniture herself.

00:04:22.230 --> 00:04:24.820
And she loved to tour
historical homes and stuff.

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:26.030
She would bring me along with her

00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:28.890
and she would do things like
organize the silverware drawer

00:04:28.890 --> 00:04:31.100
a certain way just
because it looked better.

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:34.400
And I realized that I just
sort of absorbed it all

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:36.250
and stuff that I care about now too.

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:39.110
But yes, all I want to do is
look at Architectural Digest.

00:04:39.110 --> 00:04:40.270
That's my favorite thing.

00:04:40.270 --> 00:04:43.800
- So your mom is like Martha
Stuart and Marie Kondo

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:46.660
before they existed?

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:48.770
- She kind of was, I mean, she was,

00:04:48.770 --> 00:04:51.560
I think not at that same level, but yeah,

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:53.900
she definitely was
interested in that stuff,

00:04:53.900 --> 00:04:55.510
and it just rubbed off.

00:04:55.510 --> 00:04:59.020
- I think sometimes in the
world of design, you know,

00:04:59.020 --> 00:05:02.730
things are expensive, or
they come from, you know,

00:05:02.730 --> 00:05:04.520
another person's taste,

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:07.370
and so your mom was like,
how she made things.

00:05:07.370 --> 00:05:08.890
That's like gifting in design,

00:05:08.890 --> 00:05:11.750
like the best things are
stuff of what you bring

00:05:11.750 --> 00:05:15.080
to the table, your craft,
your sense of style.

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:17.350
- Oh my gosh, yeah absolutely.

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:18.890
It's funny, when my kids were little

00:05:18.890 --> 00:05:21.008
and they, but they would bring
home all of these things,

00:05:21.008 --> 00:05:23.270
you know, they bring home so much artwork.

00:05:23.270 --> 00:05:25.240
I wouldn't, I didn't
keep all of it, you know,

00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:27.890
but I always found something
that I really loved

00:05:27.890 --> 00:05:30.780
that they made, and I'd
frame it or keep it around,

00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:32.350
and it's sort of indistinguishable

00:05:32.350 --> 00:05:33.870
from the other things that I've collected

00:05:33.870 --> 00:05:35.620
because I was even specific about that.

00:05:35.620 --> 00:05:38.030
But it has to have some
kind of a meaning to you.

00:05:38.030 --> 00:05:40.620
I mean, that's what
makes a home interesting.

00:05:40.620 --> 00:05:43.350
And I think even in terms
of furniture designers,

00:05:43.350 --> 00:05:46.590
I'm always interested
in seeing their hand,

00:05:46.590 --> 00:05:48.060
you know, their craft.

00:05:48.060 --> 00:05:50.380
That's what I love to live with.

00:05:50.380 --> 00:05:53.849
It's a representation of
people and what they do.

00:05:53.849 --> 00:05:56.682
(inspiring music)

